---
import Layout from '../layouts/BlogPost.astro';
import { getLanguage, useTranslations } from '../i18n';

const t = useTranslations(getLanguage(Astro.currentLocale));
---

<Layout title={t('nav.about')} description={t('site.description')}>
	<h2>What is SAMIZDATA?</h2>
	<p>
		SAMIZDATA is a data journalism publication focused on Eastern Europe and Central Asia, with a particular focus on Moldova. We are also a <a href="/studio/">studio</a> that helps organisations tell better stories with their data.
	</p>
	<h2>What is data journalism?</h2>
	<p>
		Data journalism is a form of journalism that uses data as a source of information. It can involve analysing large datasets, visualising data, or using data to tell stories that would be difficult to tell otherwise. See our <a href="/training/ddj/">training materials</a> for more information.
	</p>
	<p>
		Data journalism has existed since at least the 1800s. But in Eastern Europe and Central Asia, journalism is still slow to innovate, with only a handful of outlets doing any data reporting.
	</p>
	<h2>Who's running it?</h2>
	<p>
		SAMIZDATA is run by <a href="https://nicu.md/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Nicu Calcea</a>, a journalist based in London, UK and Chișinău, Moldova. His work has included data investigations at <em><a href="https://nicu.md/work?publication=Global+Witness" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Global Witness</a></em>, reporting for <em><a href="https://nicu.md/work?publication=BBC+News" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">BBC News</a></em> and the <a href="https://nicu.md/work?publication=New+Statesman" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">New Statesman</a>, and teaching data journalism at City, University of London.
	</p>
	<p>
		You can follow Nicu on <a href="https://journa.host/@nicu" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Mastodon</a>,{' '}
		<a href="https://bsky.app/profile/nicu.md" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Bluesky</a>,{' '}
		<a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/nicucalcea/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">LinkedIn</a> or{' '}
		<a href="https://www.facebook.com/nicucalcea/">Facebook</a>.
	</p>
	<h2>What’s up with the name?</h2>
	<p>
		<a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Samizdat" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Samizdat</a> was a form of self-publishing in the Soviet Union and the Eastern Bloc, largely of banned or censored texts. Data is, well, data.
	</p>
	<h2>I want to talk to you!</h2>
	<p>
		If you need <a href="/studio/">help with a data project</a>, need <a href="/training/">training for your organisation</a>, want to collaborate on a story, or just want to say hi, please <a href="/contact/">get in touch</a>.
	</p>
</Layout>
